{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://schemas.spec-kitty.ai/charter/packs/graph-shard.schema.json",
  "$defs": {
    "DRGEdge": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A typed, directed relationship between two nodes.",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^([a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*::)?(directive|tactic|styleguide|toolguide|paradigm|procedure|agent_profile|glossary_context|skill|anti_pattern|asset|template|action|mission_type|step_enhancement):[A-Za-z0-9_/.-]+$"
        },
        "target": {
          "title": "Target",
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^([a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*::)?(directive|tactic|styleguide|toolguide|paradigm|procedure|agent_profile|glossary_context|term|skill|anti_pattern|asset|template|action|mission_type|step_enhancement):[A-Za-z0-9_/.-]+$"
        },
        "relation": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Relation"
        },
        "when": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "When"
        },
        "reason": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Reason"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "source",
        "target",
        "relation"
      ],
      "allOf": [
        {
          "description": "A term is an edge endpoint only as the target of a vocabulary edge (ADR-0049 decision 4).",
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "target": {
                "pattern": "^([a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*::)?term:"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "target"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "relation": {
                "const": "vocabulary"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "DRGEdge",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DRGNode": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A single addressable doctrine artifact node.",
      "properties": {
        "urn": {
          "title": "Urn",
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^(directive|tactic|styleguide|toolguide|paradigm|procedure|agent_profile|glossary_context|skill|anti_pattern|asset|template|action|mission_type|step_enhancement):[A-Za-z0-9_/.-]+$"
        },
        "kind": {
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "directive",
            "tactic",
            "styleguide",
            "toolguide",
            "paradigm",
            "procedure",
            "agent_profile",
            "glossary_context",
            "skill",
            "anti_pattern",
            "asset",
            "template",
            "action",
            "mission_type",
            "step_enhancement"
          ]
        },
        "label": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Label"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Provenance"
        },
        "tags": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Tags",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "urn",
        "kind"
      ],
      "title": "DRGNode",
      "type": "object",
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "directive"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^directive:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "tactic"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^tactic:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "styleguide"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^styleguide:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "toolguide"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^toolguide:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "paradigm"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^paradigm:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "procedure"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^procedure:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "agent_profile"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^agent_profile:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "glossary_context"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^glossary_context:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "skill"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^skill:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "anti_pattern"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^anti_pattern:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "asset"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^asset:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "template"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^template:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "action"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^action:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "mission_type"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^mission_type:"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "const": "step_enhancement"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "urn": {
                "pattern": "^step_enhancement:"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "Relation": {
      "description": "Typed edge relations in the DRG.\n\nLineage vs. delegation vs. augmentation are three distinct concepts and\nMUST NOT be conflated (FR-001, FR-002):\n\n- ``SPECIALIZES_FROM`` (lineage): a profile derives from a parent,\n  narrowing or extending it. This is a *static composition* relation used\n  for inheritance/specialization (FR-001). A delegation is a substep's data,\n  never an edge (ADR-0064 decision 11).\n- ``ENHANCES`` / ``OVERRIDES`` (augmentation pair, FR-014, mission\n  ``charter-ux-and-org-pack-vocabulary-01KSAF14``): a pack artifact declares\n  ``enhances: <id>`` to field-merge into a built-in, or ``overrides: <id>``\n  to declare a full replacement.\n- ``REFINES`` (refinement, #2079): an artifact narrows or sharpens the\n  applicability or meaning of the target (a parent or built-in) without\n  replacing it. It is distinct from ``APPLIES`` (an action applies a\n  directive/tactic) and from ``SPECIALIZES_FROM`` (static profile/artifact\n  lineage): a refinement is a first-class, traversable relation, never a\n  synonym for ``APPLIES``. Previously the org→DRG bridge silently downgraded\n  ``refines`` to ``APPLIES`` (a dead sink); it is now preserved end-to-end.\n- ``TENSION`` / ``RECONCILES_TENSION`` / ``REJECTS`` (tension\n  vocabulary, ADR-0028 and ADR-0045): three distinct relations that must not be\n  confused with each other or with the relations above.\n\n  - ``TENSION`` is **symmetric and non-transitive**: two co-valid,\n    co-activatable rules pull against each other, and neither is\n    deprecated by the other. It is a pair class of its own, so it stands\n    beside the one structural relationship of its pair (ADR-0045 decision 1).\n    A pack writes at most one tension per unordered pair, with the side the\n    pack owns as ``source``; when the pack owns both sides, or neither, the\n    lexicographically smaller bare URN is the ``source``, so a pack may\n    declare a tension between two artifacts it holds neither of. A duplicate, a\n    reversed tension or a tension of an artifact with itself refuses the\n    pack (ADR-0045 decision 6). It must NOT be confused with supersession --\n    tension does not mean one side wins or is retired.\n  - ``RECONCILES_TENSION`` is **directional**, from an artifact to one\n    side of a tension pair. A pair counts as reconciled only when an\n    artifact in force carries this edge to BOTH sides (ADR-0045 decision 8).\n    It is never synthesized from ``TENSION`` -- it must be authored\n    explicitly.\n  - ``REJECTS`` is **directional**, from a good artefact to a marked\n    anti-pattern/smell node (``NodeKind.ANTI_PATTERN``). Unlike\n    ``TENSION`` the target is not a competing equal -- it is a\n    named bad practice, not a co-valid rule -- and unlike a supersession the\n    target was never a valid rule the rejecting artefact supersedes.\n\nEach relation names the source and target kinds it may connect (ADR-0064 decision 13). ``impacts``, ``replaces`` and ``delegates_to`` are retired (slice F): a former ``replaces`` edge is an ``overrides`` edge.",
      "enum": [
        "requires",
        "suggests",
        "applies",
        "scope",
        "vocabulary",
        "instantiates",
        "specializes_from",
        "enhances",
        "overrides",
        "refines",
        "tension",
        "reconciles_tension",
        "rejects"
      ],
      "title": "Relation",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "Top-level DRG graph document (``graph.yaml``).",
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "pattern": "^1\\.0$",
      "title": "Schema Version",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "generated_at": {
      "title": "Generated At",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "generated_by": {
      "title": "Generated By",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "nodes": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/DRGNode"
      },
      "title": "Nodes",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "edges": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/DRGEdge"
      },
      "title": "Edges",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "generated_at",
    "nodes",
    "edges"
  ],
  "title": "DRGGraph",
  "type": "object"
}
